    ["s0015","idiomatic","Take the entry into the initial or final limit for the date sought. Divide by the accumulated-degree period and discard the quotient. Multiply the remainder by the day-night difference, reduce by one hundred, and add or subtract the result to that segment's half day-and-night value to obtain the half day-and-night division for the day in question;)","Take the entry into the initial or final limit for the date sought. Divide by the accumulated-degree period and discard the quotient. Multiply the remainder by the day-night difference, reduce by one hundred, and add or subtract the result to that segment's half day-and-night value to obtain the half day-and-night division for the day in question.","s0015 ends with 為所求日半晝夜分；）—the English translation is accurate, but the fused trailing ;) is leftover from the Chinese annotation closer and should be a period only.","high","applied"],
    ["s0060","idiomatic","convert the remainder by the day circumference into days, with the leftover as parts and seconds. The result is the provisional day, parts, and seconds of nodal entry at the Heavenly Standard canonical new moon.)","convert the remainder by the day circumference into days, with the leftover as parts and seconds. The result is the provisional day, parts, and seconds of nodal entry at the Heavenly Standard canonical new moon.","s0060 ends with 入交泛日及分秒。）—an orphan closing parenthesis with no English opener; removing it leaves the correct translation.","high","applied"],
